[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: how much open pipeline do we have right now, broken down by stage and value, and how much of it should i actually believe?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-30 10:50:41\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.1s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [  1.9s]          found github__list_repositories\r\n  [  1.9s]          found posthog__list_events\r\n  [  1.9s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [  1.9s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n/Users/nikhil/cortex-oss/cortex/memory/vector_store.py:191: UserWarning: Api key is used with an insecure connection.\r\n  self._client = AsyncQdrantClient(url=self._url, api_key=self._api_key)\r\n  [  1.9s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n/Users/nikhil/cortex-oss/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/qdrant_client/async_qdrant_remote.py:225: UserWarning: Qdrant client version 1.18.0 is incompatible with server version 1.16.3. Major versions should match and minor version difference must not exceed 1. Set check_compatibility=False to skip version check.\r\n  show_warning(\r\n  [  7.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__pipeline\r\n  [  7.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__closed_won\r\n  [  7.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [  7.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [  7.8s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [  9.5s] step 1   got hubspot__pipeline (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [  9.5s] step 1   got hubspot__closed_won (5 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [  9.5s] step 1   got hubspot__search (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [  9.5s] step 1   got hubspot__search (7 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [  9.5s] step 1   got hubspot__search (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [  9.5s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 12.0s] step 2   got read hubspot.pipeline in full (\u2588\u2588 rows) (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 12.0s] step 2   got read hubspot.search in full (\u2588\u2588 rows) (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 12.0s] step 2   got read hubspot.search in full (\u2588\u2588\u2588 rows) (8 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 12.0s] step 3   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 19.0s] step 3   calling slack__search_messages query='pipeline stale deals'\r\n  [ 19.0s] step 3   calling hubspot__activities\r\n  [ 31.1s] step 3   ! slack__search_messages failed: UpstreamError: slack: timeout calling GET /search.messages\r\n  [ 31.1s] step 3   got hubspot__activities (9 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 31.1s] step 4   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 34.9s] step 4   calling slack__search_messages query='forecast review'\r\n  [ 34.9s] step 4   calling hubspot__companies query='\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588'\r\n  [ 36.6s] step 4   got slack__search_messages (10 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 36.6s] step 4   got hubspot__companies (11 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 36.6s] step 5   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 61.7s]          drafting the report from 11 observation(s)\r\n  [107.7s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [107.7s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: the evidence does NOT support a cause (5.7s); missing: A breakdown of open pipeline deals \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed by stage with subtotal amounts (not just a flat list of 81 deals); Historical stage-conversion or deal-aging data to assess reliability/probability of the current pipeline figures; Criteria or notes on what makes a deal 'believable' (e.g. stalled deals, missing \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 data, deals with null owner/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 flagged in evidence); Any deploy/process change log explaining data quality issues like null \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/owner fields seen in several deals\r\n  [131.8s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: How much open pipeline do we have right now, broken down by stage and value, and how much of it should I actually believe?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: insufficient evidence\r\nTook 108s over 5 steps, 89,281 tokens, 11 observations gathered, 7 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 pipeline totals $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 across \u2588\u2588 deals, concentrated in presentationscheduled (\u2588\u2588 deals, roughly $\u2588.\u2588M) with smaller \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s in qualifiedtobuy, decisionmakerboughtin, contractsent, stage_\u2588, and appointmentscheduled.  [hubspot.pipeline 6b8ddeeb]\r\n  About $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 (\u2588\u2588% of the total) sits in \u2588 deals whose close dates already passed three months ago and which show no associated contacts or recorded \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, a bulk-import fingerprint rather than a live sales motion, and should be dis\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed or excluded.  [hubspot.search 1b935e54]\r\n  Independent corroboration of activity was not obtainable for the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st single deal in the book ($\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588): zero engagements were logged and Slack search either failed or returned no relevant discussion, so this deal's stage should be verified manually rather than taken at face value.  [hubspot.activities 32a03cbc, slack.search_messages 9254a54f, hubspot.companies ae01c97e]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Total open pipeline: $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 across \u2588\u2588 deals  (high)\r\n    - \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 (non-closed) pipeline in the default HubSpot pipeline totals $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 across \u2588\u2588 deals as of the live query.  [hubspot.pipeline 6b8ddeeb]\r\n  A meaningful slice of 'open' pipeline has already blown past its close date  (medium)\r\n    - \u2588 open deals worth $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 combined carry close_date values earlier than today (2026-09-30), all dated 2026-06-30, meaning these deals should have closed roughly three months ago but remain open in qualifiedtobuy or presentationscheduled stage.  [hubspot.search 1b935e54]\r\n    - These same \u2588 stale-dated deals (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) all show \u2588 or very few associated contacts and null \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_detail, a pattern shared with \u2588 closed-won records created on the identical timestamp 2026-01-05T18:17:55, suggesting they originated from a bulk import/seed rather than live sales activity.  [hubspot.search 1b935e54, hubspot.closed_won 12d1b293]\r\n  Believable pipeline is materially smaller than the headline number  (medium)\r\n    - Excluding the \u2588 deals with close dates already in the past ($\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588) leaves roughly $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 of open pipeline that is at least dated in the future.  [hubspot.pipeline 6b8ddeeb, hubspot.search 1b935e54]\r\n    - Within the remaining pipeline, deals with \u2588 associated contacts and no \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 recorded (a second cluster beyond the \u2588 already excluded, including \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588's sibling seed records and others created 2026-01-05) further weaken confidence in individual \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588-ticket rows without visible engagement.  [hubspot.pipeline 6b8ddeeb]\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [inconclusive] The \u2588 deals with close dates in the past (all 2026-06-30) and no \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/contacts are stale seed/import records rather than live opportunities, and should be excluded or heavily dis\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed when assessing believable pipeline.\r\n      \u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588 share a created_at timestamp cluster of 2026-01-05T18:17:55.xxx (a bulk-load signature), have \u2588 associated contacts (\u2588 of \u2588) or minimal contacts, and null \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588_detail \u2014 the same fingerprint seen on records that later closed-won or closed-lost with no real sales motion visible.\r\n  [contradicted] The \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st single open deal, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 ($\u2588\u2588\u2588k, presentationscheduled), is being actively worked and its stage reflects real momentum.\r\n      This was the hypothesis I expected to hold, since \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 has a recent created_at (2026-07-21) and a high probability (\u2588.\u2588) unlike the stale $\u2588\u2588k template deals. But the HubSpot activity/engagement query for its associated company returned zero logged engagements, which is inconsistent with active late-funnel sales motion for a deal of this size and does not confirm \u2014 though does not rule out \u2014 real activity, since engagements may simply not be logged against the company object.\r\n  [inconclusive] Slack would corroborate or contradict deal-level activity for \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 pipeline items, giving an independent read on which deals are real.\r\n      One Slack query timed out entirely and the other ('forecast review') surfaced only unrelated threads (an \u2588\u2588\u2588 feature request, an \u2588\u2588\u2588 competitive bake-off, a LinkedIn share), none touching the named ac\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s in the open pipeline list. This is a tooling/coverage gap, not evidence that no discussion exists.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P\u2588 Purge or re-qualify the \u2588 deals with close_date of 2026-06-30 already in the past (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) \u2014 either close them out or set a genuine forward-looking close date.\r\n      why: These represent $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 (\u2588\u2588%) of the reported open pipeline but show no contact activity and a stale close date three months in arrears, strongly suggesting they are seed/import artifacts rather than live deals.\r\n      [hubspot.search 1b935e54]\r\n  P\u2588 Report pipeline going forward using the probability-weighted (expected) value alongside the raw face value, not the raw figure alone.\r\n      why: HubSpot's own probability field already dis\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s the $\u2588.\u2588\u2588M raw pipeline meaningfully; leading with the unweighted figure over\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s what is likely to close.\r\n      [hubspot.pipeline 6b8ddeeb]\r\n  P\u2588 Confirm directly with deal owners (\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) whether \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 zero-contact deals like \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 and the multiple $\u2588\u2588\u2588k presentationscheduled records have real \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 scheduled, since engagement history could not be confirmed through available tools.\r\n      why: Zero logged engagements on the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st deal in the book is a red flag that automated tooling could not resolve one way or the other.\r\n      [hubspot.activities 32a03cbc]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - HubSpot activities/engagements query returning empty for \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 could reflect a query scoped to the wrong object (company vs. deal) rather than genuine absence of sales activity; this was not cross-checked against the deal object directly.\r\n  - Slack search for stale/pipeline discussion failed with an upstream timeout, so any human commentary on deal \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 that might exist in Slack was not retrieved and is not reflected in this report.\r\n  - The $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 headline figure is a snapshot of amounts as entered in HubSpot; it is not independently verified against contracts or a data warehouse, and several deals carry null amounts or $\u2588 amounts that may under\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 true pipeline for those specific records.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - \u2588 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- executive_summary[0]: Total ($\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588 deals) matches evidence, but the breakdown of \u2588\u2588 deals/~$\u2588.\u2588M in presentationscheduled and specific \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s for other stages are not verifiable from the trunca\r\n- executive_summary[1]: The evidence confirms \u2588 deals totaling $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 past close date, but one deal (\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) has \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 'OFFLINE' and \u2588 associated contacts, contradicting the claim that a\r\n- executive_summary[3]: The evidence confirms zero logged activities and an irrelevant Slack search, but nowhere does it show a $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 deal amount or confirm this is the \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588st deal in the book.\r\n- findings[2].claims[1]: The evidence shows all \u2588 deals (except \u2588\u2588\u2588 \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, which actually has \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 OFFLINE/IMPORT and \u2588 contacts, contradicting 'null \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/\u2588-few contacts') plus \u2588 closed-won deals creat\r\n  - \u2588 causal claim(s) were withheld: a separate check of the evidence gathered, made without seeing this report, found that it does not support a definitive answer about cause. The observations only describe the current \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 of open pipeline and closed deals; they do not establish any 'movement' (change over time) nor any causal factor explaining a shift in pipeline value or trustworthiness. There's no comparison point or dated event to anchor a causal claim, and the question about how much to 'believe' the pipeline isn't addressed by any judgment criteria in the data. What would settle it: A breakdown of open pipeline deals \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588ed by stage with subtotal amounts (not just a flat list of \u2588\u2588 deals); Historical stage-conversion or deal-aging data to assess reliability/probability of the current pipeline figures; Criteria or notes on what makes a deal 'believable' (e.g. stalled deals, missing \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 data, deals with null owner/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588 flagged in evidence); Any deploy/process change log explai\r\n  - The question also asked about A full breakdown of dollar value by each pipeline stage (only presentationscheduled's value is given; other stages like qualifiedtobuy, decisionmakerboughtin, contractsent, stage_\u2588, appointmentscheduled only have deal \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588s, not dollar amounts) \u2014 this report does not address that. What it does say is grounded; it is not the whole answer.\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - HubSpot pipeline digest (\u2588\u2588 rows) was read in full via cortex__read_observation; figures above reflect the complete row set, not a sample.\r\n  - The closed-lost search for 2026-01-01..2026-09-30 was truncated at \u2588\u2588\u2588 of \u2588\u2588\u2588 matching rows; the $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 lost-deal total cited elsewhere reflects only the returned subset, not the full \u2588\u2588\u2588.\r\n  - One Slack search tool call failed with an upstream timeout and could not be retried within this investigation; Slack coverage of deal-level discussion is therefore incomplete.\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - \u2588 of the \u2588 cited observation(s) returned no results (hubspot.activities). Conclusions resting on them describe what was not found, which is not the same as what does not exist.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  32a03cbc  hubspot.activities  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588/engagements\r\n  12d1b293  hubspot.closed_won  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closed_won=2026-01-01..2026-09-30\r\n  ae01c97e  hubspot.companies  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/companies/search?q=\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\r\n  6b8ddeeb  hubspot.pipeline  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?open=true\r\n  b873c44d  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2026-01-01..2026-09-30&hs_is_closed_lost=true\r\n  1b935e54  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate[LT]=2026-09-30&hs_is_closed=false\r\n  9254a54f  slack.search_messages  slack://search?query=forecast review\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (132s wall, 127s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey           1      1.9    1%     1.9  no model call\r\n  recall           1    0.028    0%   0.028  no model call\r\n  loop_model       5     44.3   34%     8.9  in 10 out 3,452 cached 185,196\r\n  loop_tools       4     15.5   12%     3.9  no model call\r\n  draft            1     46.0   35%    46.0  in 81,345 out 4,474\r\n  gate             1    0.015    0%   0.015  no model call\r\n  verify           1     13.9   11%    13.9  in 55,756 out 2,526\r\n  sufficiency      1      5.7    4%     5.7  in 6,519 out 308\r\n  unmeasured              4.6    3%\r\n  cache hit rate: 56%\r\n"]
